    },
    {
      "id": "removal-in-linked-lists",
      "title": "Removal in Linked Lists"
    }
  ],
  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Before we get into cases, let's understand the&nbsp;<strong>core idea</strong>&nbsp;first.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When you insert into an array, the computer has to physically push elements sideways to create a gap:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Array</b> insert 99 at index 2:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115432-436859806.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Everything moves right</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115432-511736358.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115432-342138139.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A linked list never does this. Nodes sit independently in memory. To insert, you just<strong>redirect a pointer</strong>. Nobody moves. Nobody shifts. You just change where one node is pointing.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Inserting 99 between 20 and 30:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-231757991.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To insert&nbsp;<strong>99 between 20 and 30</strong>, we don’t move elements we just update pointers.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Three characters changed. That's the entire operation.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Where Can You Insert?",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Option A: At the Front",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We want to insert&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">9 at the beginning</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;of the list.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">For this, we only change pointers no shifting is needed.</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"><br></span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-270069261.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now 9 is linked to the list, but it’s not the head yet.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Option B: At the Back",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We want to add&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">74 at the end</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;of the list.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Since we don’t know where the last node is, we must&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">walk from the head to the end</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is where the walker stops.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Option C: Some where in the Middle",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We want to insert&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">99 at position 3</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, i.e., between 35 and 48.</span><br><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"><b>The key idea is</b>: we must reach the node&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">just before the position</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;(here, node 35).</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-361602323.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The walker stops at&nbsp;<strong>[35]</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now 99 points to 48.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "<p>Step 2 must happen <b>before</b> Step 3. If you do Step 3 first, you lose the reference to<code>[48]</code>forever it becomes unreachable.</p>",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "removal-in-linked-lists",
      "title": "Removal in Linked Lists",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Removal is the mirror image of insertion. Instead of linking in a new node, you&nbsp;<strong>remove a node</strong>&nbsp;by making the list skip over it.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The node isn’t physically destroyed it simply becomes unreachable. Since no pointer refers to it anymore, it effectively no longer exists.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-769341691.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-769341691.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-769341691.png",
          "alt": "Removal in Linked Lists"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "We want to remove&nbsp;<strong>48</strong>&nbsp;from the list.",
            "To do this, we don’t delete it directly we just change pointers to&nbsp;<strong>skip over it</strong>.",
            "<p>The node before 48 is&nbsp;<strong>35</strong>.&nbsp;<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We update its next pointer to point to&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">61</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">instead of 48.</span></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Where Can You Remove?",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115433-440307130.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Option A: Remove from the Front",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We want to delete the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">first node (22)</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, which is currently the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">HEAD</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406115434-901002923.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "In a linked list, the only way to access nodes is through pointers.<br>Right now, HEAD is the only pointer that can reach 22."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When we do:&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "HEAD = HEAD.next",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">HEAD stops pointing to 22 and starts pointing to&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">35</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Option B: Remove from the Back",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We want to delete the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">last node (61)</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116262-565357569.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "But we can’t directly reach the last node’s previous pointer, so we must find the node&nbsp;<strong>just before it</strong>."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Start from HEAD and move forward until you reach the node where:<br><code>next.next == null</code>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This means you are at&nbsp;<strong>48</strong>, the node just before 61.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Option C: Remove from the Middle",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We want to delete a node with a <strong>specific value (35)</strong>. To do this, we first find the node <strong>just before the target</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<br><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116264-162884757.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Start from HEAD and move forward until:<br><code>walker.next.data == 35</code>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This means the walker stops at&nbsp;<strong>22</strong>&nbsp;(just before 35).",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116264-524818927.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Insertion at Front:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We add the new node at the beginning by pointing it to the current head and then updating the head. <strong>No traversal is needed</strong>, so it works in <strong>O(1)</strong> time.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Insertion at Back:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We first walk through the list to reach the last node, then attach the new node at the end. <strong>Traversal is required</strong>, so the time complexity is <strong>O(n)</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Insertion in Middle:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We move to the node just before the target position and insert the new node by adjusting pointers. <strong>Requires traversal</strong>, so it takes <strong>O(n)</strong> time.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Removal from Front:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We simply move the head to the next node, removing the first element. <strong>No traversal is needed</strong>, so it is <strong>O(1)</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Removal from Back:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We traverse to the second-last node and set its next to null, removing the last node. <strong>Traversal is required</strong>, so it takes <strong>O(n)</strong> time.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Removal from Middle:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We move to the node just before the target and make it skip the node to be deleted. <strong>Requires traversal</strong>, so the time complexity is <strong>O(n)</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "items": [],
          "url": "",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "{\"headers\":[\"Operation\",\"Position\",\"Steps Involved\",\"Time\"],\"rows\":[[\"Insert\",\"Front\",\"Point new → head, move HEAD\",\"O(1)\"],[\"Insert\",\"Back\",\"Walk to tail, attach new node\",\"O(n)\"],[\"Insert\",\"Middle\",\"Walk to predecessor, rewire\",\"O(n)\"],[\"Remove\",\"Front\",\"Move HEAD forward\",\"O(1)\"],[\"Remove\",\"Back\",\"Walk to second-last, cut next\",\"O(n)\"],[\"Remove\",\"Middle\",\"Walk to predecessor, skip target\",\"O(n)\"]]}",
          "text": ""
